{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#779","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#779","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#779\",\"parent_revision\":\"c5df7d52420b8461906d2c31b5400dfa5aadb307\",\"root_revision\":\"3c8b5f31160ab82553b6f549f93874f9f9c25e2ea5093f2d18456cf4846b7dee\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n**Current state**: The SAM workflow has three implicit phases (planning via `/add-new-feature`, execution via `/implement-feature`, quality gates via `/complete-implementation`) but no explicit plan-level phase field in the data model. Running `uv run sam status P{N}` returns task counts (`total_tasks`, `by_status`, `ready_tasks`, `blocked_tasks`, `completion_pct`) but does not report which workflow phase the plan is in. The orchestrator infers phase from task status counts (e.g., \\\"all tasks COMPLETE\\\" means ready for quality gates), but this inference is implicit and undocumented. File: `plugins/python3-development/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` \u2014 the Progress Loop section queries `sam status` and `sam ready` but has no mechanism to read or write a plan-level phase. File: `packages/sam_schema/` \u2014 no workflow phase field exists in the Plan model.\\n\\n**Target state**: The `sam_schema` Plan model includes an optional `phase` field with defined values: `planning`, `executing`, `quality-gates`, `complete`, `blocked`. The `sam status P{N}` output includes `\\\"phase\\\": \\\"executing\\\"` in its JSON response. The `/add-new-feature` skill sets phase to `planning` on plan creation. The `/implement-feature` skill sets phase to `executing` when entering the progress loop. The `/complete-implementation` skill sets phase to `quality-gates` on entry and `complete` on success.\\n\\n**Measurable signal**: Run `uv run sam status P{N}` on any active plan \u2014 output JSON contains a `phase` field with one of the defined values. Read any plan YAML file \u2014 frontmatter contains `phase: executing` (or equivalent). The `/implement-feature` SKILL.md references the phase field in its Progress Loop section.\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Snapshot: SAM Plan-level workflow phase field in data model\\nDate: 2026-04-23\\nGoal: Add a `phase` field to the Plan model so workflow phase is explicit and machine-readable rather than inferred from task counts.\\n\\nConditions:\\n1. Plan model location | AVAILABLE | plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py \u2014 Plan class\\n2. implement-feature SKILL Progress Loop | AVAILABLE | plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md \u2014 queries sam status and sam ready\\n3. sam status MCP tool output schema | AVAILABLE | SAM MCP server; sam_plan(action='status') returns task counts but no phase field\\n4. add-new-feature and complete-implementation SKILL phase write points | AVAILABLE | plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/ and complete-implementation/ (write locations)\\n5. Phase transition logic | DERIVABLE | phase values and transition rules: planning \u2192 executing \u2192 quality-gates \u2192 complete | blocked; needs definition\\n\\nAVAILABLE count: 4\\nDERIVABLE count: 1\\nMISSING count: 0\\n\\nDecision: APPROVED \u2014 implementation path clear; phase values and transition rules defined in description.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **sam: plan-level workflow phase field in data model** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/research-agent-patterns/the-delegation.md \u2014 pattern: Agency State Machine (explicit phase transitions)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-18\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-23)\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- [ ] `sam_schema` Plan model includes optional `phase` field with literal values: `planning | executing | quality-gates | complete | blocked`\\n- [ ] `sam_plan(action='status')` response JSON includes `\\\"phase\\\"` field reflecting the current value (or `null` for legacy plans without phase)\\n- [ ] Any plan YAML file written by `/add-new-feature` contains `phase: planning` in frontmatter\\n- [ ] `/implement-feature` SKILL Progress Loop writes `phase: executing` when entering the loop\\n- [ ] `/complete-implementation` writes `phase: quality-gates` on entry and `phase: complete` on success\\n- [ ] `uv run ty check plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/` \u2014 zero errors on modified files\\n- [ ] New test: `sam_plan(action='status')` on a plan with `phase: executing` returns `\\\"phase\\\": \\\"executing\\\"` in output\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/models.py` \u2014 Plan model (add phase field)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` \u2014 Progress Loop (write phase: executing)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md` \u2014 plan creation (write phase: planning)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md` \u2014 quality gates (write phase: quality-gates / complete)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md` \u2014 document phase field\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/` \u2014 new or extended test for phase field\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs an **orchestrator running `/implement-feature` or `/complete-implementation`**, I want **a `phase` field on the SAM Plan model** so that **I can read the current workflow phase from the plan directly instead of inferring it from task status counts**.\\n\",\"digest\":\"61d26ca837bdd89e48e7798818bfbaba8990b165d8a6acc75e675971404ba119\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPgyzHQ\"}"}